From: challoc <noreply@chainguard.dev>
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] db, object: no write to a key's value on overwrite,
 delete or its last decrRefCount when no module observes it

Redis 8.10.3 (tag 8.10.3, commit 1a2574ce1551d3de6e0b4a56756c0fdbc6659e4f).
Independent of patches 1/6 to 4/6 and of the allocator: it applies to stock
8.10.3. The Redis counterpart of contrib/valkey/0003, with two differences
Redis needs.

Every overwrite (dbSetValue) and every delete (dbGenericDelete: DEL,
UNLINK, expiration, eviction) wrote the old value's refcount twice: the
pin around moduleNotifyKeyUnlink (incrRefCount, then decrRefCount),
because a module's key event callback may call RM_StringDMA, whose
dbUnshareStringValue can free the value, and then the final
decrRefCount, which decrements the count to 0 before it frees the
object. While a fork child is alive (BGSAVE, BGREWRITEAOF, full sync)
either write copies the page holding the kvobj.

- The pin is taken only when module code runs: the key carries module
  metadata (keyMetaOnUnlink, which Valkey does not have, runs under the
  same pin), a module listens for the key event, or the value is a
  module type. moduleNotifyKeyUnlink returns at once otherwise; module.c
  keeps a count of key event listeners (subscribe, unsubscribe, unload)
  for moduleKeyUnlinkObserved.
- decrRefCount frees an object whose count is 1 without writing the
  count first, and decrements it otherwise. Valkey's decrRefCount already
  does this.

Measured in a develop session (8 vCPU, 31 GiB, amd64), 10M keys with
64-byte values (raw strings in Redis: its embstr limit is 44 bytes), 1M
random keys changed during a 60 s BGSAVE, rdb_last_cow_size in MiB:

                     jemalloc  +this   challoc  +this   challoc fork epoch (0006)  +this
  SET                1141      1141    1175     1175    616                        235
  DEL                 623       620     651      646    619                        237

Alone it saves nothing on Redis: a freed kvobj's slot is handed out again
to the next command's argument objects, which write the page anyway. With
challoc's fork epoch (patch 6/6), which hands out no block freed during
the save and places new objects on pages the child does not share, it is
what takes the copy from 616 to 235 MiB on SET and from 619 to 237 on DEL.

tests/unit/moduleapi/postnotifications.tcl gains a test that the listener
count follows module unload and load (the key event reaches a reloaded
module, and overwrites and deletes of every encoding work without one).
The existing "Test removed key event" in hooks.tcl covers the pinned path
with RM_StringDMA.

---
 src/db.c                                   |   21 +++++++++++++-------
 src/module.c                               |   16 +++++++++++++++
 src/object.c                               |    8 +++++++
 src/server.h                               |    1 +
 tests/unit/moduleapi/postnotifications.tcl |   30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 68 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/db.c b/src/db.c
index 3aa7216..9f802ad 100644
--- a/src/db.c
+++ b/src/db.c
@@ -609,8 +609,12 @@ static void dbSetValue(redisDb *db, robj *key, robj **valref, dictEntryLink link
         /* On overwrite, discard module metadata excluding expire if set */
         newKeyMetaBits &= KEY_META_MASK_EXPIRE;
         /* RM_StringDMA may call dbUnshareStringValue which may free val, so we
-         * need to incr to retain old */
-        incrRefCount(old);
+         * need to incr to retain old while module code runs. With no module
+         * metadata on the key and no module observing the unlink, no module
+         * code runs, and the pin is skipped: it would write old's refcount,
+         * copying its page while a fork child shares it. */
+        int pin = getModuleMetaBits(old->metabits) || moduleKeyUnlinkObserved(old);
+        if (pin) incrRefCount(old);
 
         /* Free related metadata. Ignore builtin metadata (currently only expire) */
         if (getModuleMetaBits(old->metabits)) {
@@ -623,8 +627,8 @@ static void dbSetValue(redisDb *db, robj *key, robj **valref, dictEntryLink link
          * callback of the module. */
         moduleNotifyKeyUnlink(key,old,db->id,DB_FLAG_KEY_OVERWRITE);
         /* We want to try to unblock any module clients or clients using a blocking XREADGROUP */
-        signalDeletedKeyAsReady(db,key,old->type);
-        decrRefCount(old);
+        signalDeletedKeyAsReady(db,key,oldtype);
+        if (pin) decrRefCount(old);
         /* Because of RM_StringDMA, old may be changed, so we need get old again */
         old = dictGetKV(*link);
     }
@@ -873,8 +877,11 @@ int dbGenericDelete(redisDb *db, robj *key, int async, int flags) {
             streamKeyRemoved(db, key, kv);
 
         /* RM_StringDMA may call dbUnshareStringValue which may free kv, so we
-         * need to incr to retain kv */
-        incrRefCount(kv); /* refcnt=1->2 */
+         * need to incr to retain kv while module code runs. When none runs
+         * (no module metadata, no module observing the unlink) the pin is
+         * skipped, as in dbSetValue: it would write kv's refcount. */
+        int pin = getModuleMetaBits(kv->metabits) || moduleKeyUnlinkObserved(kv);
+        if (pin) incrRefCount(kv); /* refcnt=1->2 */
         /* Metadata hook: notify unlink for key metadata cleanup. */
         if (getModuleMetaBits(kv->metabits)) keyMetaOnUnlink(db, key, kv);
         /* Tells the module that the key has been unlinked from the database. */
@@ -883,7 +890,7 @@ int dbGenericDelete(redisDb *db, robj *key, int async, int flags) {
         signalDeletedKeyAsReady(db,key,type);
         /* We should call decr before freeObjAsync. If not, the refcount may be
          * greater than 1, so freeObjAsync doesn't work */
-        decrRefCount(kv);
+        if (pin) decrRefCount(kv);
 
         /* Because of dbUnshareStringValue, the val in db may change. */
         kv = dictGetKV(*link);
diff --git a/src/module.c b/src/module.c
index ff646d5..e1f388e 100644
--- a/src/module.c
+++ b/src/module.c
@@ -452,6 +452,8 @@ typedef struct RedisModuleEventListener {
 } RedisModuleEventListener;
 
 list *RedisModule_EventListeners; /* Global list of all the active events. */
+/* How many of them listen for REDISMODULE_EVENT_KEY (moduleKeyUnlinkObserved). */
+static int keyEventListeners = 0;
 
 /* Data structures related to the redis module users */
 
@@ -13018,6 +13020,7 @@ int RM_SubscribeToServerEvent(RedisModuleCtx *ctx, RedisModuleEvent event, Redis
     /* Modify or remove the event listener if we already had one. */
     if (ln) {
         if (callback == NULL) {
+            if (el->event.id == REDISMODULE_EVENT_KEY) keyEventListeners--;
             listDelNode(RedisModule_EventListeners,ln);
             zfree(el);
         } else {
@@ -13032,6 +13035,7 @@ int RM_SubscribeToServerEvent(RedisModuleCtx *ctx, RedisModuleEvent event, Redis
     el->event = event;
     el->callback = callback;
     listAddNodeTail(RedisModule_EventListeners,el);
+    if (event.id == REDISMODULE_EVENT_KEY) keyEventListeners++;
     return REDISMODULE_OK;
 }
 
@@ -13200,6 +13204,7 @@ void moduleUnsubscribeAllServerEvents(RedisModule *module) {
     while((ln = listNext(&li))) {
         el = ln->value;
         if (el->module == module) {
+            if (el->event.id == REDISMODULE_EVENT_KEY) keyEventListeners--;
             listDelNode(RedisModule_EventListeners,ln);
             zfree(el);
         }
@@ -13229,7 +13234,18 @@ void processModuleLoadingProgressEvent(int is_aof) {
 
 /* When a key is deleted (in dbAsyncDelete/dbSyncDelete/setKey), it
 *  will be called to tell the module which key is about to be released. */
+/* Whether moduleNotifyKeyUnlink(kv) runs module code: a module listens for
+ * the key event, or kv is a module type (its unlink callbacks). When it
+ * does not, moduleNotifyKeyUnlink neither reads nor writes kv, and the
+ * callers need not retain kv around it (see dbSetValue and dbGenericDelete:
+ * that retain writes kv's refcount, which copies the page holding it while
+ * a fork child, BGSAVE, AOF rewrite or full sync, shares it). */
+int moduleKeyUnlinkObserved(kvobj *kv) {
+    return keyEventListeners != 0 || kv->type == OBJ_MODULE;
+}
+
 void moduleNotifyKeyUnlink(robj *key, kvobj *kv, int dbid, int flags) {
+    if (!moduleKeyUnlinkObserved(kv)) return;
     server.allow_access_expired++;
     server.allow_access_trimmed++;
     int subevent = REDISMODULE_SUBEVENT_KEY_DELETED;
diff --git a/src/object.c b/src/object.c
index 603ed7f..0c0c032 100644
--- a/src/object.c
+++ b/src/object.c
@@ -649,7 +649,11 @@ void decrRefCount(robj *o) {
             o->type, o->encoding, o->refcount);
     }
 
-    if (--(o->refcount) == 0) {
+    /* The last reference frees the object without writing its count first:
+     * a write would copy the page holding the object while a fork child
+     * (BGSAVE, AOF rewrite, full sync) shares it, on every overwrite and
+     * delete of a key. */
+    if (o->refcount == 1) {
         /* Fast path for embedded strings: no inner allocation to free, and we
          * can compute the alloc size to hint jemalloc for a faster deallocation. */
         if (o->type == OBJ_STRING && o->encoding == OBJ_ENCODING_EMBSTR && !o->iskvobj) {
@@ -685,6 +689,8 @@ void decrRefCount(robj *o) {
             }
         }
         zfree(alloc);
+    } else {
+        o->refcount--;
     }
 }
 
diff --git a/src/server.h b/src/server.h
index b4285df..6a615e1 100644
--- a/src/server.h
+++ b/src/server.h
@@ -3271,6 +3271,7 @@ void moduleUnblockClient(client *c);
 int moduleBlockedClientMayTimeout(client *c);
 int moduleClientIsBlockedOnKeys(client *c);
 void moduleNotifyUserChanged(client *c);
+int moduleKeyUnlinkObserved(kvobj *kv);
 void moduleNotifyKeyUnlink(robj *key, kvobj *kv, int dbid, int flags);
 size_t moduleGetFreeEffort(robj *key, robj *val, int dbid);
 size_t moduleGetMemUsage(robj *key, robj *val, size_t sample_size, int dbid);
diff --git a/tests/unit/moduleapi/postnotifications.tcl b/tests/unit/moduleapi/postnotifications.tcl
index 31a4669..6bf512b 100644
--- a/tests/unit/moduleapi/postnotifications.tcl
+++ b/tests/unit/moduleapi/postnotifications.tcl
@@ -216,4 +216,34 @@ tags "modules external:skip" {
             close_replication_stream $repl
         }
     }
+
+    start_server {} {
+        test {Key event listener count follows module unload and load} {
+            r module load $testmodule with_key_events
+            r set k1 v1
+            r set k1 v2
+            assert_equal {k1} [r lrange before_overwritten 0 -1]
+
+            # With the only key event listener gone, overwrites and deletes
+            # of every encoding skip the module notification and still work.
+            r module unload postnotifications
+            r del before_overwritten
+            r set k1 123
+            r set k1 v3
+            r set k2 [string repeat x 100]
+            r set k2 456
+            r del k1 k2
+            r set k3 abcd px 1
+            after 10
+            assert_equal 0 [r exists k1 k2 k3 before_overwritten before_deleted]
+
+            # Loaded again, the listener is counted again and notified.
+            r module load $testmodule with_key_events
+            r set k1 v1
+            r set k1 789
+            r del k1
+            assert_equal {k1} [r lrange before_overwritten 0 -1]
+            assert_equal {k1} [r lrange before_deleted 0 -1]
+        }
+    }
 }
